    "text": "<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/465095-1.JPG\" style=\"width: 260px; height: 223px;\" /></p><p>We know&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>μN</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>mg</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>cosθ</mi></math></p><p>Now, since wedge is in equilibrium,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>sinθ</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">μ</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>mg</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>cosθ</mi><mo>)</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">μ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">θ</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">θ</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p>",
